The plugin was a portable manifest (plugin.json), one mcp.json entry, a skill and a
5400-line Python bridge between Hermes and MCP for Unity (CoplayDev/unity-mcp 10.3.0).
The bridge started that server itself, wrapped its ~409 operations into nineteen unity_*
tools, and made every change a plan: plan_batch measured the editor, apply_plan ran the
steps in order after one approval, a second question covered deletes, editor code and
unsaved work, every file the plan did not name was put back, and a separate measurement
decided whether play mode, a compile or a test run had really succeeded.

This rewrite keeps the four things a model needs to reach that same editor from a
Nodecode session -- the tool list, one call, a plan and its apply -- and speaks MCP over
HTTP to MCP for Unity's own endpoint in Lisp through nlk:http, so no Python, no uvx, no
stdio child and no bridge process sit between them. The plan keeps the original's
shape: every step and its arguments are shown before anything runs, a plan carries an
id, runs once, only the newest plan runs, and it expires; the first failing step stops
the plan and names the step. The path checks the original made before planning are kept,
as far as an argument's own text can be judged without the project: no .., no hidden
file, no key or credential file, no absolute path, no deleting Assets, Packages or
ProjectSettings, and no File/Quit. The skill's guidance is the cell's manual topic,
(help :unity), and each tool's argument list is its declared schema.

What was left out: the editor-transport preference read from EditorPrefs, the uvx
stdio child and every warm-up it did (the cell uses the endpoint the section names);
the editor-state fingerprint a plan was made against; the before-and-after walk of the
project that put back files a plan did not name, and the second question for risky
plans, because this cell has no chat surface of its own to ask in; the per-op side
effect table the original extracted from MCP for Unity's C# source; the done-measurement
of play mode, compiles, test rows and build output (the cell reports each step's own
answer and stops on the first refusal, and says so); and the resources read. Nothing of
the original is vendored.
